  "note": "Three hand-authored personas for the Employee Offboarding Checklist validator. validateChecklist(state) walks 38 declarative rules (27 mandatory, 11 optional) in catalogue order; a rule 'fires' when the item is OUTSTANDING. Outcome: 'incomplete' if any mandatory+blocker rule fired, else 'partial' if any rule at all fired, else 'complete'. completionPercent = round1(mandatorySatisfied / 27 x 100), so a checklist can be 100% and still 'partial' (only optional items outstanding). Quirks verified: yes/no/na equipment items count 'na' as satisfied (notYesOrNa) but yes/no items treat '' and 'no' identically (notYes); REF-001 fires only on '' (an explicit 'no' consent is NOT outstanding); EXI-003 is gated on interviewCompleted === 'yes', so a declined interview never fires it. Flags are SPLIT: form-app.js calls detectAdditionalFlags(state) with the state only (no grader result), mirrored by flagsArgs [\"state\"]; flags are stable-sorted high > medium > low and FLAG-AC-003 keys off dataDownloadAuditPerformed !== 'yes' independently of the rules. The 'timestamp' key is added by form-app.js, not the grader. Regenerate expected with: bin/test-personas employee-offboarding-checklist --update",
